<x-layouts.site title="Factual record policy" description="Horsefax preserves documented facts about a horse's life: identifiable facts, historical events, official results and supporting documents, each with its source. It does not publish opinions.">
    <x-page-header eyebrow="Our commitment" title="Factual horse histories." lede="Our goal is not to tell you what to think about a horse. It's to help you understand what can be documented about its history." />
    <div class="wrap py-16 prose-hf max-w-[46em]">
        <p>Horsefax exists to preserve and connect documented information about a horse's life. Our records focus on identifiable facts, historical events, official results and supporting documentation. Every entry identifies its source and whether it has been verified.</p>
        <p>Horsefax does not publish personal reviews, subjective evaluations of temperament, opinions about suitability, or unsupported claims about a horse's abilities or character. Where information is disputed, incomplete or unverified, Horsefax says so rather than presenting uncertainty as fact.</p>

        <h2>What belongs on a record</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>The horse competed at a particular event, and how it placed.</li>
            <li>The horse earned a title or award from an association.</li>
            <li>The horse was in training with a named trainer or at a named facility for a stated period.</li>
            <li>The horse was offered or sold at a named sale, with the result the sale reported.</li>
            <li>A veterinary examination took place on a date, with the report issued by the named veterinarian.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What does not</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>"Beginner-safe," "wonderful temperament," "difficult" or "dangerous."</li>
            <li>"Finished reiner" or other training-level judgments without an objective standard.</li>
            <li>"Guaranteed sound" or any medical conclusion or prediction.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Professional and veterinary records</h2>
        <p>Professionals may contribute documented historical information within their areas of expertise, with the owner's authorization and their own name attached. A verified professional is a verified <em>source</em>; it doesn't make everything they submit a verified <em>fact</em>, and entries are labeled accordingly.</p>
        <p>Veterinary records are clinical records, not opinions: Horsefax keeps them as attributed records of the veterinarian who issued them (for example, "Examination performed June 12, 2025; report issued by Dr. Smith"), shared only with permission. Horsefax never declares a veterinary conclusion to be its own verified finding.</p>

        <h2>Sources, not endorsements</h2>
        <p>An authenticated sale listing proves the listing existed, not that every claim in it was accurate. A published result is shown as published. The same standard applies to owners, trainers, breeders, veterinarians and sale companies.</p>
        <p>If something on a record is wrong, use "Something wrong here?" on the record, or see <a href="{{ route('record-corrections') }}">how corrections work</a>.</p>
    </div>
</x-layouts.site>
